{'symbol': 'FITB', 'date': '2022-10-05 17:47:00', 'title': 'FIFTH THIRD FOUNDATION DONATES $500,000 FOR HURRICANE RELIEF IN FLORIDA', 'text': 'CINCINNATI--(BUSINESS WIRE)--THE FIFTH THIRD FOUNDATION HAS CONTRIBUTED $500,000 TO SUPPORT RELIEF EFFORTS FOR THOSE IMPACTED BY HURRICANE IAN, WHICH MADE LANDFALL IN FLORIDA ON SEPT. 28. TIM SPENCE, PRESIDENT AND CEO OF FIFTH THIRD BANCORP, SAID THE $500,000 DONATION TO FIVE LOCAL ORGANIZATIONS AIMS AT BRINGING RELIEF TO THE PEOPLE IMPACTED AND THE THOUSANDS WHO CONTINUE TO GRAPPLE IN THE AFTERMATH OF THE TRAGEDY. IN ADDITION, FIFTH THIRD BANK HAS DEPLOYED ITS FIFTH THIRD FINANCIAL EMPOWERMENT'}